First Author: Lipkova
Title: Deep learning-enabled assessment of cardiac allograft rejection from endomyocardial biopsies
Source number: 31  ￼

Very short summary: This study developed CRANE, a deep-learning system for automated assessment of cardiac allograft rejection from endomyocardial biopsy whole-slide images. Five key findings were: (1) the internal U.S. development dataset included 5,054 WSIs from 1,690 patient biopsies, with additional external cohorts from Turkey and Switzerland; (2) on the U.S. hold-out test set, the model detected overall rejection with AUC 0.962 and accuracy 0.899; (3) it classified acute cellular rejection, antibody-mediated rejection, and Quilty B lesions with AUCs 0.958, 0.874, and 0.939, respectively; (4) it differentiated low-grade from high-grade rejection with AUC 0.833; and (5) in a human reader study, the AI system showed non-inferior performance to conventional assessment while reducing interobserver variability and assessment time. Figures 1–5 and the main results text were used directly for this extraction.  ￼

