	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The internal U.S. cohort was split into 70% training, 10% validation, and 20% hold-out testing. Since the U.S. dataset contained 5,054 WSIs, this corresponds to about 3,548 training WSIs and about 1,011 hold-out WSIs; adding the external Turkish and Swiss test cohorts gives 1,717 + 123 + 1,011 = about 2,851 total test WSIs, but for the strict held-out internal test field I report the internal U.S. holdout only as 1,011 if only internal is desired. However, because the prompt asks for test/validation size and the paper emphasizes rigorous external testing, I instead used the clearly reported external test cohorts separately in the narrative and note this ambiguity. Tissue segmentation, patching, transfer learning, and multi-magnification fusion were clearly described. Class imbalance was handled partly by balanced cohort partitioning rather than conventional reweighting; hence “Other.” Missing-data handling and code availability were not reported in the retrieved text.  ￼

